// workers/src/blocks-calculators.js
//
// Renderer for the "calculators_hub" block type — the 14-calculator hub
// (affordability, mortgage payment, LTT, HST rebate, etc.) as a page
// builder block, built from the same source as the standalone
// /calculators page (calculators.html). No `data_source` needed — this
// block ignores `data` and (mostly) ignores `props`; everything it needs
// is baked into its own markup or fetched client-side.
//
// IMPORTANT — single instance per page only. This is a single big
// self-contained mini-app (hash-based routing between the 14 calculators,
// its own PDF generator, its own lead-capture flow) with hardcoded DOM
// ids throughout (`cfgModal`, `hubGrid`, `heroIcon`, ...) — none of them
// are namespaced per render, unlike map_split_search's `mapId` counter.
// Placing this block twice on the same page (or twice in the same preview
// render) will collide and break. Its CSS, however, IS fully scoped under
// `.calculators-hub` (every selector rewritten from the standalone page's
// global `*`/`body`/bare-tag rules), so unlike the ids, the CSS is safe —
// it will not leak onto the rest of whatever page this block sits on.
//
// Regulatory settings (stress test buffer, GDS/TDS limits, CMHC premium
// tiers, LTT rebates) are NOT props on this block — they're fetched
// client-side straight from Supabase (`calculators_config`, slug
// `global-settings`) the same way the standalone page does, and are
// edited centrally in the admin's Calculators tab, not per-block.

